eegdev
------------------------------------------
eegdev is a library that provides an interface for accessing various EEG (and
other biosignals) acquisition systems in a unified way. The interface has been
designed in order to be both flexible and efficient. The device specific part
is implemented by the means of plugins which makes adding new device backend
fairly easy even if the library does not support them yet officially.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libeegdev-devel-0.2-1bl1
  libeegdev0-0.2-1bl1
  libexpat1-2.10.0-1
  libusb1.0-1.0.21-1
  libusb1.0-devel-1.0.21-1
  libxdffileio-devel-0.3-1bl4
  libxdffileio0-0.3-1bl4
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  bison-3.8.2-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  flex-2.6.4-2
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libexpat-devel-2.10.0-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  libusb1.0-devel-1.0.21-1
  libxdffileio-devel-0.3-1bl4
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://sourceforge.net/projects/eegdev/

Canonical download:
  mirror://sourceforge/eegdev/eegdev-0.2.tar.bz2

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack eegdev-0.2-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./eegdev-0.2-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/eegdev-0.2-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/eegdev-0.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libeegdev0-0.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libeegdev-devel-0.2-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

